,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kra-Dai languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kra–Dai_languages,"In 1942, Benedict placed three Kra languages (Gelao, Laqua (Qabiao), and Lachi) together with Hlai in a group that he called ""Kadai"", from ka, meaning ""person"" in Gelao and Laqua and dai, a form of a Hlai autonym. [10] Benedict's (1942) ""Kadai"" group was based on his observation that Kra and Hlai languages have Austronesian -like numerals.",Lachi,Kra-Dai
1,Lachi (artist) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lachi_(artist),"Lachi (whose legal name is Lachi Music) [1] is an American recording artist, songwriter, touring performer, record producer, media personality, author, and disability culture advocate based in New York City. [2]",Lachi,Kra-Dai
